{"name":"Slippery Soap","hex":"#efedd8","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"slippery","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a surface, having low friction, often due to being covered in a non-viscous liquid, and therefore hard to grip, hard to stand on without falling, etc.","Evasive; difficult to pin down."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slippery"},{"term":"soap","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A metallic salt derived from a fatty acid, commonly used in cleaning products.","Some other substance, often a detergent or another surfactant, able to mix with both oil and water, used for cleaning."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To apply soap to in washing.","To cover, lather, or in any other manner treat with soap, often as a prank."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soap"}],"entries":[{"title":"Soap","blocks":[{"text":"Soap is a salt of a fatty acid used for cleaning and lubricating products as well as other applications. In a domestic setting, soaps, specifically \"toilet soaps\", are surfactants typically used for washing, bathing, and other types of housekeeping. In industrial settings, soaps are used as thickeners, components of some lubricants, emulsifiers, and catalysts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Handmade_soap_cropped_and_simplified.jpg/330px-Handmade_soap_cropped_and_simplified.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soap","wikidata":"Q34396"},{"title":"Lavender (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lavender is a light shade of purple or violet. It applies particularly to the color of the flower of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Lavandula_fields.jpg/330px-Lavandula_fields.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lavender_(color)","wikidata":"Q2468392"}],"i